#N 10-cell infinite growth
#O Paul Callahan, 1997
#C A single ten-cell cluster that grows without bound by turning into a
#C block-laying switch engine; ten is the proven minimum population for
#C infinite growth.
#C Verified by the Emergence Lab verifier (B3/S23, unbounded grid): linear
#C growth: +16 cells every 144 generations from generation 564 on.
#C Source: Life Lexicon Release 29, entry "infinitegrowth", diagram 1
